feat 1.0

# SPEC-ADPKMS-001 — the KMS service adapter (@mmmnt/feat-adapter-kms, built on the official
# @aws-sdk/client-kms). Agreed by founder ruling 58a4ac88; fault counts (every integration catalog
# entry declares ["reset"], unobserved is accepted evidence, firedFaults is not implemented) by
# founder ruling c7af7871.
#
# Driven through adapters/kms/fixtures/probe.mjs (part of the build, inside touches, not shipped)
# against a local-kms container (nsmithuk/local-kms) the TEST starts, with dummy credentials and
# its dummy account and region; nothing here needs AWS. `ObserveKms { script, emulator?,
# settleTimeoutMs? }` creates one adapter per namespace named in the script and runs a
# space-separated script. `<alias>` is relative: the namespace's alias is `alias/<ns>/<alias>`.
# Steps:
#   setup:<ns> / observes:<ns>
#   seed:<ns>:<alias>                adapter.seed(): a symmetric key with that alias, before the window
#   createkey:<ns>:<alias>           the SYSTEM creates a symmetric key and the alias
#   createkeyraw:<name>              the SYSTEM creates a key with no namespace tag and no namespaced alias
#   disable / schedule / rotate : <ns>:<alias>   the SYSTEM disables the key, schedules its deletion, enables rotation
#   tag:<ns>:<alias>:<k>:<v>         the SYSTEM tags the key
#   deletealias:<ns>:<alias>         the SYSTEM deletes the alias
#   encrypt:<ns>:<alias>             the SYSTEM encrypts with the key (a cryptographic use)
#   start / peek / stop / settle / reset : <ns>
#   read:<ns>[:<alias>]              adapter.read() with or without an expect hint
#   fault:<ns>:UseKey.<FAULT>:<alias>[:once|:times2|:reset]
#   fired:<ns>
# The trace carries the record count for window and read steps, settle true/false,
# `observes:a=<diff>/<state>`, a refused use `encrypt:a!DISABLED` (DISABLED, KMS_INVALID_STATE,
# NOT_FOUND). `last` is the last peek or stop as `TYPE:key` joined by comma, sorted by key;
# a key's identity is its first namespaced alias (relative), else its Name tag, else its KeyId.
# `readVia` is DescribeKey (a hint with an alias) or ListKeys.
#
# Verified (DESIGN.md has the sources): local-kms documents no change feed or audit stream, and
# AWS KMS state is read with ListKeys, DescribeKey, ListAliases, ListResourceTags and
# GetKeyRotationStatus, all of which the SDK and local-kms offer. So the diff is a snapshot of
# key state; `observes` says `snapshot`. A snapshot sees what changed key STATE, tags, aliases or
# rotation; it cannot see a cryptographic use (Encrypt, Decrypt, Sign, GenerateDataKey), which
# leaves nothing behind. AWS documents KMS as eventually consistent, so settle vouches only for the
# emulator, which the options must declare.

spec SPEC-ADPKMS-001 "KMS adapter: snapshot diff of key state, namespace, settle, reset and faults"
context Toolchain
aggregate Adapters
type infrastructure
status agreed

construct:
  handler at adapters/kms/src/index.ts
  touches adapters/kms/**
  needs SPEC-RT-002
  needs SPEC-FPX-001
  Declare `observes = { diff: "snapshot", state: true }` and the fault catalog `{ UseKey:
  { DISABLED: ["reset"], PENDING_DELETION: ["reset"], ALIAS_NOT_FOUND: ["reset"] }, Connection:
  { Timeout: ["reset"], ConnectionReset: ["reset"], Partition: ["reset"] } }` (Connection only with `options.proxy`).
  Options: `endpoint` (or `endpointEnv`; absent = the SDK default, which this draft does not
  exercise), `region`, `auth` (env-var NAMES), `emulator`
  ("local-kms" or absent), `settleTimeoutMs`, `proxy`.
  Namespace: received from the runner (SPEC-RT-006) as the config's top-level `namespace`, never an option; the probe maps each script label (a, b) to the namespace `s` + 12 hex of sha256(label), and `raw=<value>` passes a value as is.
  Namespace use: a key is in the namespace when it carries the tag `feat:namespace` = `<ns>` or any
  alias starting `alias/<ns>/`; an alias is in it when it starts so. Reported aliases and the
  identity drop that prefix; `feat:*` tags are never reported.
  startCapture(): snapshot the namespace. peekCapture()/stopCapture(): snapshot again and diff by
  identity: INSERT, MODIFY (key state, enabled, description, rotation, user tags, aliases),
  REMOVE; CapturedRecord { type, key, payload: { keyState, enabled, keySpec, keyUsage,
  description, rotationEnabled, tags, aliases }, timestamp: the capture time }, sorted by key.
  settle(): false with no window open, false unless `options.emulator` is "local-kms"; otherwise
  true (the emulator answers reads from the state its writes already changed). It writes nothing.
  read(query): the snapshot's records; with `query.expect` entries that give an alias, DescribeKey
  on that alias instead of listing; fault effects (a disabled key) are reported as they are.
  seed(records): CreateKey with the namespace tag and CreateAlias, before the window.
  reset(): for every key in the namespace delete its aliases, remove the namespace tag, then
  ScheduleKeyDeletion (7 days, the minimum), disarm faults first (EnableKey, CancelKeyDeletion
  then EnableKey, CreateAlias); close the window.
  fault(UseKey.*, alias): DISABLED = DisableKey on the aliased key; PENDING_DELETION =
  ScheduleKeyDeletion; ALIAS_NOT_FOUND = DeleteAlias (remembering the key). The alias must exist.

enforce:
  rejects NAMESPACE_INVALID when the namespace does not match ^s[0-9a-f]{12}$, the pattern the runner derives (SPEC-RT-006); defensive, the runner never passes another
  rejects KMS_UNREACHABLE when the endpoint does not answer at setup
  rejects FAULT_TARGET_MISSING when a fault names an alias that does not exist
  rejects FAULT_UNSUPPORTED when a fault is not in the catalog, or when its count is not one the fault declares
  capture and read are restricted to keys tagged with, or aliased under, the namespace
  the namespace tag and prefix are never reported
  the diff is a snapshot of key state and cannot see a cryptographic use of a key
  settle resolves true only for a declared emulator, whose reads follow its writes
  settle resolves false when no window is open or the endpoint is not a declared emulator
  firedFaults is not implemented because KMS reports no request it refused
  reset removes the namespace from every key, schedules their deletion and restores every faulted key first

contract:
  input ObserveInput
  response ObserveResult
  error ObserveError

scenario outline "a namespace that does not match the runner's pattern is refused":
  when: ObserveKms { script: <script> }
  predict rejection NAMESPACE_INVALID:
    response ERR ObserveError { code: "NAMESPACE_INVALID", detail: matching <detail> }
    filesystem has []
  examples:
    | script         | detail   |
    | "setup:raw=Orders" | "Orders" |
    | "setup:raw=a/b"    | "a/b"    |
    | "setup:raw=S0599e33863c1" | "S0599e33863c1" |
    | "setup:raw=s0599e33863c"  | "s0599e33863c" |

scenario "an endpoint that does not answer is a configuration error at setup":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a", emulator: "unreachable" }
  predict rejection KMS_UNREACHABLE:
    response ERR ObserveError { code: "KMS_UNREACHABLE", detail: matching "endpoint" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "the adapter declares snapshot diff and state":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a observes:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a observes:a=snapshot/true" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a window reports keys created and changed, seeds excluded":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a seed:a:signing start:a createkey:a:orders disable:a:signing stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult {
      trace: "setup:a seed:a start:a createkey:a disable:a stop:a=2",
      last: "INSERT:orders,MODIFY:signing"
    }
    filesystem has []

scenario "rotation and tags are changes of state":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a seed:a:one seed:a:two start:a rotate:a:one tag:a:two:team:core stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult {
      trace: "setup:a seed:a seed:a start:a rotate:a tag:a stop:a=2",
      last: "MODIFY:one,MODIFY:two"
    }
    filesystem has []

scenario "deleting a key's only alias changes its identity, so it reads as one removal and one insertion":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a seed:a:three start:a deletealias:a:three stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a seed:a start:a deletealias:a stop:a=2" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a key scheduled for deletion is a change, not a removal":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a seed:a:one start:a schedule:a:one stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a seed:a start:a schedule:a stop:a=1", last: "MODIFY:one" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "two namespaces never see each other's keys":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a setup:b start:a start:b createkey:a:orders createkey:b:orders createkey:b:billing stop:a stop:b" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult {
      trace: "setup:a setup:b start:a start:b createkey:a createkey:b createkey:b stop:a=1 stop:b=2",
      last: "INSERT:billing,INSERT:orders"
    }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a key with no namespace tag and no namespaced alias is nobody's effect":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a start:a createkeyraw:stray stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a start:a createkeyraw stop:a=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a cryptographic use of a key leaves nothing for a snapshot to see":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a seed:a:signing start:a encrypt:a:signing stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a seed:a start:a encrypt:a stop:a=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a peek reports the window's records and consumes nothing":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a start:a createkey:a:orders peek:a peek:a stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult {
      trace: "setup:a start:a createkey:a peek:a=1 peek:a=1 stop:a=1",
      last: "INSERT:orders",
      peekEqualsStop: true
    }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a peek with no window open is empty":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a createkey:a:orders peek:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a createkey:a peek:a=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "settle vouches for the emulator, whose reads follow its writes":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a start:a createkey:a:orders settle:a stop:a", emulator: "local-kms" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a start:a createkey:a settle:a=true stop:a=1", last: "INSERT:orders" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "settle vouches on an empty window, which is how an absence is proven":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a start:a settle:a stop:a", emulator: "local-kms" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a start:a settle:a=true stop:a=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "settle declines when the endpoint is not a declared emulator, because KMS is eventually consistent":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a start:a createkey:a:orders settle:a stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a start:a createkey:a settle:a=false stop:a=1", last: "INSERT:orders" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "settle declines when no window is open":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a settle:a", emulator: "local-kms" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a settle:a=false" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a read given an alias describes that key":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a seed:a:orders seed:a:billing read:a:orders" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a seed:a seed:a read:a:orders=1", readVia: "DescribeKey" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a read given no hint lists the namespace and no other":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a setup:b seed:a:orders seed:b:orders read:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a setup:b seed:a seed:b read:a=1", readVia: "ListKeys" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "reset takes the namespace's keys out of the namespace and leaves the other one alone":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a setup:b seed:a:orders seed:b:orders reset:a read:a read:b" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a setup:b seed:a seed:b reset:a read:a=0 read:b=1" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a use of a disabled key is refused when DISABLED is armed":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a seed:a:signing fault:a:UseKey.DISABLED:signing start:a encrypt:a:signing stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a seed:a fault:a:UseKey.DISABLED start:a encrypt:a!DISABLED stop:a=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a use of a key pending deletion is refused when PENDING_DELETION is armed":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a seed:a:signing fault:a:UseKey.PENDING_DELETION:signing start:a encrypt:a:signing stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a seed:a fault:a:UseKey.PENDING_DELETION start:a encrypt:a!KMS_INVALID_STATE stop:a=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a use through a missing alias is refused when ALIAS_NOT_FOUND is armed":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a seed:a:signing fault:a:UseKey.ALIAS_NOT_FOUND:signing start:a encrypt:a:signing stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a seed:a fault:a:UseKey.ALIAS_NOT_FOUND start:a encrypt:a!NOT_FOUND stop:a=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "reset leaves no fault behind, so a fresh key under the same alias is usable":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a seed:a:signing fault:a:UseKey.PENDING_DELETION:signing reset:a seed:a:signing start:a encrypt:a:signing stop:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a seed:a fault:a:UseKey.PENDING_DELETION reset:a seed:a start:a encrypt:a stop:a=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a fault cannot be armed on an alias that does not exist":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a fault:a:UseKey.DISABLED:ghost" }
  predict rejection FAULT_TARGET_MISSING:
    response ERR ObserveError { code: "FAULT_TARGET_MISSING", detail: matching "ghost" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "KMS reports no request it refused, so firedFaults is not offered":
  when: ObserveKms { script: "setup:a seed:a:signing fault:a:UseKey.DISABLED:signing fired:a" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "setup:a seed:a fault:a:UseKey.DISABLED fired:a=unobserved" }
    filesystem has []

scenario outline "a fault the binding cannot produce faithfully is refused before it does anything":
  when: ObserveKms { script: <script> }
  predict rejection FAULT_UNSUPPORTED:
    response ERR ObserveError { code: "FAULT_UNSUPPORTED", detail: matching <detail> }
    filesystem has []
  examples:
    | script                                                         | detail       |
    | "setup:a seed:a:signing fault:a:UseKey.DISABLED:signing:once"  | "once"       |
    | "setup:a seed:a:signing fault:a:UseKey.THROTTLED:signing"      | "THROTTLED"  |
    | "setup:a seed:a:signing fault:a:Sign.DISABLED:signing"         | "Sign"       |
